<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Token Radar — pre-token protocols ranked by implied launch value</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="app.css">
</head>
<body>
<a class="skip" href="#board">Skip to the board</a>
<header class="top">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Token launch radar · model radar-2</p>
    <h1>Which protocol launches next — and what it would be worth</h1>
    <p class="lede">Every protocol in a sealed DefiLlama snapshot that records no token and is not a
    wrapped, staked or bridged product of one that already trades, ranked by the implied value of
    its launch. Each row carries a farm plan: what to do, what it costs, how long it takes.</p>
    <dl class="stats" id="stats"></dl>
  </div>
</header>
<nav class="tabs wrap" aria-label="Views">
  <button type="button" data-tab="board" class="active" aria-current="page">Board</button>
  <button type="button" data-tab="live">Live tokens</button>
  <button type="button" data-tab="model">How the model works</button>
</nav>
<main class="wrap">
  <section id="view-board" class="view">
    <div class="controls" role="search">
      <label>Search <input id="q" type="search" placeholder="name, slug or category" autocomplete="off"></label>
      <label>Category <select id="category"><option value="">All categories</option></select></label>
      <label>Chain <select id="chain"><option value="">All chains</option></select></label>
      <label class="check"><input id="watchlist" type="checkbox"> Watchlist only</label>
      <label>Sort <select id="sort">
        <option value="value">Implied value</option>
        <option value="tvl">TVL</option>
        <option value="growth">7-day growth</option>
        <option value="age">Age</option>
        <option value="name">Name</option>
      </select></label>
    </div>
    <p class="count" id="count" aria-live="polite"></p>
    <section id="detail" class="detail" hidden></section>
    <div class="tablewrap">
      <table id="board">
        <thead><tr>
          <th data-sort="value" class="num sorted">Rank</th>
          <th data-sort="name">Protocol</th>
          <th data-sort="category">Category</th>
          <th>Chains</th>
          <th data-sort="tvl" class="num">TVL</th>
          <th data-sort="growth" class="num">7d</th>
          <th data-sort="age" class="num">Age</th>
          <th data-sort="value" class="num">Implied value</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody id="rows"></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">Implied value is this entry's model, not a market price and not make.fun's
    claim. A protocol “records no token” when the snapshot records none for it — DefiLlama's
    record is not proof it has none.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="view-live" class="view" hidden>
    <h2>Already trading — shown for calibration, never ranked</h2>
    <p>These protocols already have a token that trades. Their market cap over TVL is what
    prices the board: each category's multiple is the median of its live-token peers.</p>
    <div class="tablewrap">
      <table id="livetable">
        <thead><tr>
          <th>Protocol</th><th>Category</th><th class="num">TVL</th>
          <th class="num">Market cap</th><th class="num">Mcap / TVL</th><th class="num">7d</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody id="liverows"></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="view-model" class="view" hidden>
    <h2>How the model works</h2>
    <p>One function scores every protocol. Nothing is hard-coded by name: the same four
    multipliers price every row, and the category multiples are computed from this snapshot's
    own live-token protocols.</p>
    <ol class="formula">
      <li><strong>Category multiple</strong> — the median market-cap-over-TVL of the live-token
      protocols in the same category (at least 3 peers, else the median over all live-token
      protocols), clamped to 0.05 – 1.00.</li>
      <li><strong>Growth</strong> — the 7-day TVL change, clamped to −50% … +100%, at a weight of
      0.6: multiplier 1 + 0.6 × growth.</li>
      <li><strong>Maturity</strong> — 0.60 + 0.40 × min(age, 1095 days) / 1095. A protocol that
      has run longer with no token is worth more; an unknown listing date counts as 365 days.</li>
      <li><strong>Chains</strong> — 1 + 0.02 per extra chain, up to 5 extra chains.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="formula-line">implied value = TVL × category × growth × maturity × chains, rounded to whole dollars.</p>
    <h3>Peer multiples by category</h3>
    <div class="tablewrap">
      <table id="peertable">
        <thead><tr><th>Category</th><th class="num">Live peers</th><th class="num">Multiple</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody id="peerrows"></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <h3>What the board leaves out</h3>
    <p>Bridges, canonical bridges, liquid staking, liquid restaking, restaked BTC and CEX
    protocols are out: they are wrapped or staked products of a token that already trades, not
    launches of their own. So are versioned pools (a name ending in V2, v2 or 2.0), names carrying
    the word wrapped, staked or staking, and protocols named after an exchange. The snapshot is
    sealed at its fetch date and never moves; the board is a reading of it, not a prediction of
    whether or when any token is issued.</p>
  </section>
</main>
<footer class="wrap">
  <p>Snapshot: DefiLlama protocols, fetched 2026-11-14, 758 protocols at or above $5M TVL.
  Watchlist floor $50M. Built for make.fun's “Build the best token launch radar” bounty.</p>
</footer>
<script src="../data.js"></script>
<script src="app.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```
